    "result_text": "Build succeeds and the test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\n**Addressed the main finding** \u2014 duplicated knowledge in `DisposableEmailValidator`:\n- `BLOCKED_LABELS` is now derived from `BLOCKED_DOMAINS` (stripping each domain's final TLD) rather than being a parallel hand-maintained literal. `BLOCKED_DOMAINS` is now the single source of truth, so adding/removing a blocked domain automatically updates the adjacency rule. Added the `java.util.stream.Collectors` import for the new stream.\n\n**Left the minor nit as-is** \u2014 `isRiskFlag(Owner)` keeps its name. It's consistent with the surrounding boolean predicates (`isBulkSignupDay`, `isCityApproachingCapacity`, `isCityOverSoftCapacity`), and the reviewer flagged it as optional/fine to leave.\n\nAcceptance behaviour is unchanged (the derivation produces the exact same label set \u2014 `mailinator`, `tempmail`, `guerrillamail`), and the full test suite passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
